{"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"protocol","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"DistributedTargetInvocationEncoder","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/com.apple.Swift\/documentation\/Distributed\/DistributedTargetInvocationEncoder\/SerializationRequirement","preciseIdentifier":"s:11Distributed0A23TargetInvocationEncoderP24SerializationRequirementQa","text":"SerializationRequirement","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Forming an invocation","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Forming-an-invocation"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"On the sending-side an instance of an invocation is constructed by the runtime,","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and calls to: ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"recordGenericSubstitution"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"recordArgument","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"recordReturnType","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":",","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"recordErrorType"},{"text":", and finally ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"doneRecording"},{"text":" are made (in this order).","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the return type of the target is ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Void"},{"text":" the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"recordReturnType"},{"text":" is not invoked.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"If the error type thrown by the target is not defined the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"recordErrorType"},{"text":" is not invoked.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"An invocation implementation may decide to perform serialization right-away in the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"code":"record...","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" invocations, or it may choose to delay doing so until the invocation is passed","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"to the ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"remoteCall"},{"text":". This decision largely depends on if serialization is allowed to happen","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"on the caller’s task, and if any smarter encoding can be used once all parameter calls have been","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"recorded (e.g. it may be possible to run-length encode values of certain types etc.)"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Once encoded, the system should use some underlying transport mechanism to send the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"text":"bytes serialized by the invocation to the remote peer.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Decoding an invocation","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Decoding-an-invocation"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Since every actor system is going to deal with a concrete invocation type, they may","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"implement decoding them whichever way is most optimal for the given system.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Once decided, the invocation must be passed to ","type":"text"},{"code":"executeDistributedTarget","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":"which will decode the substitutions, argument values, return and error types (in that order)."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Note that the decoding will be provided the specific types that the sending side used to preform the call,","type":"text"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"so decoding can rely on simply invoking e.g. "},{"code":"Codable","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" (if that is the "},{"code":"SerializationRequirement","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":") decoding"},{"typ